%%%
# Synthetic laboratory histogram fit

Two supplied integrated-bin component shapes describe a three-bin assay.
Inputs are independent nonnegative strengths, not fractions. Outputs are the
Poisson log likelihood followed by the three expected measured bin counts.
No prior is imposed; a host optimizer can maximize outputs[1].
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"
a = load_module("../main.flatppl")
strengths = elementof(cartpow(nonnegreals, 2))
templates = rowstack([[0.6, 0.1], [0.3, 0.3], [0.1, 0.6]])
background = [1.0, 1.0, 1.0]
counts_data = [17, 14, 12]
expected = a.combine(templates, strengths) .+ background
sampling_law = a.poisson_model(templates, strengths, background)
log_likelihood = logdensityof(sampling_law, counts_data)
inputs = strengths
outputs = [log_likelihood, expected[1], expected[2], expected[3]]
